<!-- Writing Journal 3a: original and revised, side by side — review build -->
<Vertical id="wj3_review_root">

<!--
---
description: "Writing Journal 3a, twice: the original group chat and the revised one, as two tabs of one activity. A review build for the course owner, not a student-facing activity — it is reachable only at its own /wj3-review route and is deliberately absent from wj_course. Both tabs read and write the same student state and pull their screens from the same activity bank (writing_journal2_activities_part1.olx), so the only difference a reviewer sees is the difference that is actually there."
category: writing_journal2
index: 92.1
lang: en-Latn-US
---
-->

<!-- WHAT THIS WRAPPER IS FOR.

     Writing Journal 3a is being revised. This file puts the two versions in
     adjacent tabs so they can be read against each other in the browser: the
     "Original" tab mounts the original's own Circle tab (wj2_circle_tab,
     defined in writing_journal2a_sba_part1.olx), and the "Revised" tab mounts
     a second chat column, wj3_chat, running writing_journal3a_dialogue.chatpeg
     against its own pane, wj3_sidebar.

     BOTH VERSIONS SHARE STATE. The screens in the right-hand pane are the same
     blocks in both tabs — one activity bank, one set of input ids — so a quiz
     answered in the Original tab is answered in the Revised tab too. That is
     the point: what differs between the tabs is the conversation, not the work.
     Each chat keeps its own place in its own script (wj2_chat and wj3_chat are
     separate blocks), and each drives its own pane.

     THE ORIGINAL IS UNTOUCHED. Nothing here edits the original journal: it is
     referenced, not copied. writing_journal2a_sba_part1.olx, its chatpeg, and
     the activity bank are the shipping content, and wj2a_sba_part1 remains the
     activity students reach through wj_course.

     THIS WRAPPER AND THE wj3_ BLOCKS ARE THE SCAFFOLD. Every id prefixed wj3_
     — this file's blocks, the revised chatpeg's pane target, and the
     revised-only screens later commits will add to the activity bank — belongs
     to the revised version alone. Blocks still prefixed wj2_ are shared by both
     versions. When the review finishes and the revised version takes over, the
     wj3_ blocks are what gets promoted and this wrapper is what gets deleted.

     The namespace is shared (everything under sba-journals/ parses as one), so
     wj3_ ids must not collide with wj2_ ones. -->

<Cast cast="characters.cast" id="wj3_review"
      title="Writing Journal 3a — original and revised"
      launchable="true">
  <Tabs id="wj3_review_tabs">

    <!-- Tab 1: the original, exactly as it ships. wj2_circle_tab carries its own
         SplitPanel, its own chat (wj2_chat), its own pane (wj2_sidebar) and the
         nine Flash/FocusAction cue Triggers that sit outside that SplitPanel. -->
    <Vertical id="wj3_original_tab" title="Original">
      <Use ref="wj2_circle_tab" />
    </Vertical>

    <!-- Tab 2: the revised conversation, driving its own pane. Same geometry as
         the original's Circle tab (38/62, 460px of chat) so the two tabs differ
         only in their content.

         No cue Triggers here yet. The original's nine are a marked HACK — they
         compare a pane value written as a qualified ref against a bare name and
         need DefinitionKey() on both sides — and the fix is cues riding the
         embed itself. Re-cueing the revised pane is the last step of the review,
         after the screens themselves settle, so nothing is copied over now. -->
    <Vertical id="wj3_circle_tab" title="Revised">
      <SplitPanel id="wj3_sba_split" sizes="38, 62">
        <StartPane>
          <Chat id="wj3_chat"
                src="writing_journal3a_dialogue.chatpeg"
                cast="characters.cast"
                height="460px" />
        </StartPane>
        <EndPane>
          <Vertical id="wj3_current_activity" title="Current Activity">
            <UseHistory id="wj3_sidebar" initial="wj2_welcome" />
          </Vertical>
        </EndPane>
      </SplitPanel>
    </Vertical>

    <!-- Tabs 3 and 4 are the original's own, referenced the way 3a and 3b
         reference them. They are shared, so they need no revised twin: the
         record and the character list are the same work either way. -->
    <Vertical id="wj3_journal_tab" title="My Journal">
      <Use ref="wj2_artifact" />
    </Vertical>

    <Vertical id="wj3_people_tab" title="Characters">
      <Use ref="wj2_circle_members" />
    </Vertical>

    <!-- Tab 5: the revised export. The revised journal is one part, so its whole
         record fits on one page, and nothing here teleports to this tab — the
         revised chat's closing line names it and the student clicks it. -->
    <Vertical id="wj3_print_tab" title="Print &amp; Submit">
      <Use ref="wj3_print" />
    </Vertical>

  </Tabs>
</Cast>

<!-- ============================================================
     REFERENCED CONTENT BLOCKS
     ============================================================ -->

<!-- Loader: pull Writing Journal 3a into scope so the bare refs above
     (wj2_circle_tab, wj2_artifact, wj2_circle_members — all defined there, and
     the artifact through that file's own loader) resolve. src= must NOT go on a
     rendered <Use> (it leaks onto the inlined block -> "Invalid attributes:
     src"), so the loader carries it here instead. -->
<Use ref="wj2_circle_tab" src="writing_journal2a_sba_part1.olx"/>

</Vertical>
